        "heading_XWQhHz": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "text": "Similar yet different",
            "heading_tag": "h1",
            "heading_tag_html": "h2",
            "text_color": "",
            "gradient": ""
          }
        },
        "richtext_bUiMCC": {
          "type": "richtext",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>We think the Toniebox is a great product. It’s got millions of children listening to stories, the figures are lovely to collect, and plenty of families we know love theirs. The Toniebox 2 also does more than play stories: with the Tonies app you can set a sleep timer and sunrise alarm, record your own stories onto a Creative-Tonie and play Tonieplay games.&nbsp;</p><p>Voxblock is simply built around a different idea. There’s no wi-fi, no downloads and no app to set up. Each story lives inside its own book, so your child just adds the story and presses play. If you want connected features and collectable figures, the Toniebox is well worth a look. If you’d rather keep things simple and screen-free, we think you’ll love Voxblock. We’ve put this comparison together in a fair spirit, to help parents choose what suits their family, and not to knock anyone else’s product. If anything here is out of date or not quite right, let us know and we’ll happily correct it.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
